chip ym2610
clock 8000000
samples 30000
mem adpcm-b opn-b.bin
fidelity min
# ADPCM-B on the YM2610, in 256-byte units, which forces external mode and
# refuses recording: the sine once, its end-of-sample flag in bit 7 of the
# extended status, reset and masked through 0x1C, the ramp repeating, a
# write asking for CPU playback and recording (both refused), and the
# level and pan.
0 w 0 11 1 c0 0 12 1 00 0 13 1 00 0 14 1 03 0 15 1 00 0 19 1 00 0 1a 1 c0 0 1b 1 d0 0 10 1 80
200 r 2
800 r 2
1400 r 2
2000 r 2
2600 r 2
3200 r 2
3800 r 2
4400 r 2
5000 r 2
5600 r 2
6200 r 2
6800 r 2
7400 r 2
8000 r 2
8600 r 2
9000 w 0 1c 1 80  # reset and mask the ADPCM-B flag
9200 r 2
9500 w 0 1c 1 00
9800 r 2
10000 w 0 11 1 80 0 12 1 10 0 13 1 00 0 14 1 1f 0 15 1 00 0 1a 1 90 0 10 1 90  # the ramp, repeating, left
10400 r 2
11000 r 2
11600 r 2
12200 r 2
12800 r 2
13400 r 2
14000 r 2
14600 r 2
15200 r 2
15800 r 2
16400 r 2
17000 r 2
17600 r 2
18000 w 0 10 1 40 0 18 1 55  # record asked: refused, external forced
18200 r 2
18800 r 2
19000 w 0 11 1 40 0 12 1 30 0 13 1 00 0 14 1 3f 0 15 1 00 0 10 1 00 0 10 1 80  # the chirp, right
19400 r 2
20000 r 2
20600 r 2
21200 r 2
21800 r 2
22400 r 2
23000 r 2
23600 r 2
24200 r 2
24800 r 2
25400 r 2
26000 r 2
26600 r 2
27200 r 2
27800 r 2
28400 r 2
29000 r 2
29600 r 2
